# yamlboard runtime scratch
# `.yamlboard/` itself is tracked - it IS the board, and a clone that arrived
# without it cannot tell who holds which file. Only the two per-machine
# artefacts are ignored: the advisory flock and the scratch of an interrupted
# save. Both are matched at any depth so the checked-in fixture under
# examples/ behaves exactly like a real store at the repo root.
**/.yamlboard/.lock
**/.yamlboard/.tmp-*.yaml

# editors / os
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
